Thanks!

@Parcly-Taxel, in future PRs, could you please link the related automated PR (#42655) in the PR description? That additional context would help to notice that this is a shortcoming in the automation. Thanks!

maintainer merge

AI (OpenAI Codex) was used extensively for this PR. It was used to:

- investigate the original TODO and reproduce why `dsimp` failed;
- explore and discard several possible fixes;
- identify the semireducible diagram/forgetful-functor boundaries involved;
- design and implement the final `ProfiniteGrp` API simplification and `ProfiniteCompletion.lift` proof changes;
- run the relevant Lean builds and direct compilation checks; and
- draft the commit message and PR description.

The final changes were reviewed through the resulting diff and verified locally with `lake build Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Category.ProfiniteGrp.Completion` (1892 jobs), direct compilation of `Completion.lean`, and `git diff --check`.

One file experienced slowdowns (+48%) from this PR, though im not sure its necessarily worth investigating:
[#rss > Significant commits to mathlib4 @ 💬](https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/116290-rss/topic/Significant.20commits.20to.20mathlib4/near/617653626)
@gaetanserre @RemyDegenne

> It is not clear to me at all an autoformatter would include this

We can find out by asking the author:
@hargoniX is the autoformatter going to include changes like this PR from the start? (My impression certainly is that this would be *possible* to implement, it is a kind of syntax canonisation pass after all.)

@themathqueen

> and the other one could be `norm_map_mul_star_le`?

I switched to your names but added `cauchy_scwharz_...` for discoverability.

@AlyciaBHZ Some general remarks:
* Please resolve comments (by clicking on the "Resolve conversation" button) when you have dealt with them. It is then easier to see which discussion points are still open.
* `omega` should be replaced by `lia` (see [#lean4 > Completing &#96;omega&#96; with a verified QF_LIA backend @ 💬](https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Completing.20.60omega.60.20with.20a.20verified.20QF_LIA.20backend/near/611883379); there are probably better references in the Zulip). `lia` ("linear integer arithmetic") is a part of `grind` that is supposed to deal with everything that `omega` can solve.

@YaelDillies Looks like these are leftover from #3731 and #30191, and there are more name mismatches such as
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/62f3addadd0f6b58ac6ddd85c0ceec85012d64a9/Mathlib/Algebra/Category/Grp/Adjunctions.lean#L49
scattered across files. Maybe you could ask some AI to find and fix them all?

@thorimur 

> One possible objection to this PR is that those variables show what is allowed to be available in these sections for future lemmas, and so should not necessarily be removed

Yeah, I basically mentioned this in Zulip, but I think the fact that there is a perf impact by having them there makes it clear that we should remove them rather than keep them 'just in case'
